1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
This video introduces the range pull function for you.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Starting from the 2025 version, when you press and pull the clothing in the simulation mode,

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,000
the area and strength of the support for pull are defined, and the exact adjustment is made according to the needs.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Now it shows several application scenarios for range pull.

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:25,000
For single-layer clothing, we can make small-range twist details through the range pull function.

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:29,000
You can also make relatively large-range suit back adjustment.

7
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:36,000
When you modify the posture, you can use the range pull to adjust the waist with a multi-layer structure.

8
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Next, let's take a look at how to use it.

9
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:43,000
To use the range pull, we need to open the simulation first.

10
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Once the simulation is opened, select the move tool to switch to the small-handle point pull tool.

11
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:54,000
At this time, we press the point pull tool for two seconds, and we can see the tool group.

12
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Press the range pull tool to move the mouse to the 3D window of the clothing.

13
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:03,000
You can see that on the basis of the original grip, two new circles have been added.

14
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:05,000
This is our range brush.

15
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:09,000
It can help you directly understand the range of the influence of the range pull.

16
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:13,000
In addition, we can also see that there is a range pull window setting.

17
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:17,000
The window setting is divided into two main contents, range and options.

18
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:19,000
First, let's look at the range.

19
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:23,000
The reduction type below the range is controlled by the shape of the pull effect.

20
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:27,000
You can switch it to a curve or a straight line.

21
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:33,000
The range of soft selection and the degree of reduction separately control the range of influence when the pull is pulled and the range of the center point.

22
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:38,000
The smaller inner circle in the two circles indicates the area where the pull effect is most directly applied.

23
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:43,000
As the effect is radiated outward, the strength gradually decreases, resulting in a smooth natural reduction.

24
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:46,000
The range of soft selection is controlled by the area affected by the pull.

25
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:51,000
As the value increases, the size of the two circles on the clothing will also be expanded accordingly.

26
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:55,000
The default value is 200, and it can be adjusted within the range of 1 to 500.

27
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:01,000
The degree of reduction is controlled from the core area of the pull to the maximum range of influence.

28
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:05,000
The default value is 0, and it can be adjusted within the range of 2 to 2.

29
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:09,000
The chart area below can help you understand more objectively.

30
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:18,000
When the reduction type is a curve, the pull selection area is not a single pull, but a smoother, rounder, and wider shape.

31
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:21,000
Next, let's use the curve as an example to see the effect.

32
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:23,000
Let's use the default value of the pull sleeve first.

33
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:26,000
Change the soft selection range to 250.

34
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:28,000
Turn to the back of the suit to pull.

35
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:33,000
You will see that the pull effect is more effective in the area where the same core is defined.

36
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:37,000
This time, let's set the soft selection range to 500 and pull the clothing.

37
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:42,000
Compared to before, the area covered by the inner circle and the outer circle is now twice as wide.

38
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:44,000
You can pull a larger area.

39
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:47,000
Now let's set the value to be the smallest.

40
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:49,000
Then pull the panel again.

41
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:51,000
The soft selection range is only 1 mm.

42
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:53,000
This allows us to make a very small range of pull.

43
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:56,000
Next, we will change the soft selection range to 200.

44
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:59,000
And set the reduction degree to the smallest value to 2.

45
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Then pull.

46
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:03,000
In this case, the inner circle almost overlaps with the outer circle.

47
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:08,000
The pull effect is evenly distributed in a larger area, rather than concentrated on a specific point.

48
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:13,000
Finally, let's set the maximum value to 2 and pull the clothes again.

49
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:17,000
Through the chart below, you can see that the pull force is highly concentrated at a specific point.

50
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:20,000
This means that accurate operation is performed in small areas.

51
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:24,000
Next, we will adjust the reduction degree to 1.

52
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:26,000
The reduction type is modified to a straight line.

53
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:31,000
The straight line allows you to define a smaller and more detailed core area to be squeezed.

54
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:37,000
After switching to the straight line option, you will notice that the picture becomes sharper and sharper.

55
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:43,000
At this time, when you pull the clothes, you will find that the selection range of the core area is narrower and more accurate than the curve line.

56
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:45,000
So you can control the pull correctly.

57
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:49,000
You can choose the reduction type according to your preferences.

58
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:50,000
Next, let's take a look.

59
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:53,000
How to display and control the pull selection area.

60
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:58,000
At the bottom of the option, the range measurement method defines how to calculate the selection area from the actual point.

61
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:01,000
It is divided into two types, the surface and the straight line.

62
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:06,000
In the surface mode, the pull effect is only applicable to the surface of a selected layer within the specified range.

63
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:09,000
Even if there are multiple layers here, it is the same.

64
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:18,000
However, when the pull and the strip are sewed together, any soft selection range that is defined and the area within the reduction range will be affected at the same time.

65
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:23,000
The straight line option allows you to pull all the sheets within a certain distance.

66
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:27,000
Whether the selected sheet is sewed together with the sheets of other layers,

67
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:33,000
when you use this option to pull the sheet, you will see that all the sheets within the defined range are affected at the same time.

68
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:38,000
The range brush display can help you to understand the range of the pull function more objectively.

69
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:41,000
You can also turn off the range brush display here.

70
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:47,000
Now let's take a look at the use of each range measurement method.

71
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:51,000
The range brush display is only used for the effect of pulling the area when selecting the selected sheet.

72
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:55,000
As you can see, whether it is the surface or the straight line,

73
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:59,000
as a range measurement method and only used for selecting the selected sheet,

74
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:04,000
when the range brush is turned over, it will only affect the currently selected turned over sheet.

75
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:07,000
When you want to pull a specific sheet in the given work process,

76
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:12,000
no matter which range measurement method you choose, this option is very useful.

77
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:15,000
Next, when the full weight function is used,

78
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:18,000
the range brush display will display the pull area in green.

79
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:22,000
If you turn off this option, the range brush display will no longer display the area in green,

80
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:25,000
but it will not affect the effect of the range brush.

81
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:29,000
The range brush is not only used to adjust the overall effect of the clothes,

82
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:33,000
but it can also help to quickly adjust various details such as knotting and knotting.

83
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:38,000
First, re-position the fixed needle and prepare for the knotting.

84
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:43,000
Then select the range brush tool and adjust the range and the degree of reduction according to the area size of the brush.

85
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:48,000
After the setting is complete, turn to the appropriate angle,

86
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:51,000
pull the clothes to complete the knotting details.

87
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:57,000
After achieving the desired effect, delete the fixed needle and continue to simulate.

88
00:05:57,000 --> 00:06:00,000
Then the introduction of the range brush function is here,

89
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:05,000
I hope this function can help you quickly adjust the ideal clothing effect.

